# Task Roadmap: Pruning Engine

## Version 2: OpenCV Pruning Proof of Concept (Offline, Standalone)

### Phase 1: Context Checks
- [x] Confirm OpenCV and Pillow are installed and importable in the venv (`python -c "import cv2, PIL"`)
- [x] Confirm `test_screenshot.png` from v0.2 exists and is a valid, non-corrupted image
- [x] Collect 5–10 additional sample screenshots across different page types (search results, product page, cart) for broader testing
- [x] Create a `pruning/` module folder to keep this logic isolated from the agent code

### Phase 2: Grayscale & Thresholding
- [x] Write a function to convert a screenshot to grayscale
- [x] Apply binary thresholding to separate content from background
- [x] Save the thresholded mask image to disk for visual inspection
- [x] Tune the threshold value until background (white/solid) areas are cleanly separated from content (text/UI)

### Phase 3: Contour Detection
- [x] Run `cv2.findContours` on the thresholded image
- [x] Filter out contours below a minimum area (to ignore noise/specks)
- [x] Draw bounding boxes over detected contours on a copy of the original image
- [x] Visually verify by eye that boxes correctly wrap text blocks and UI elements

### Phase 4: Crop, Stitch & Measure
- [x] Crop out background rows/columns outside detected bounding boxes
- [x] Stitch remaining content blocks into a single dense collage using Pillow
- [x] Build a standalone `prune(image) -> pruned_image` function with a clean input/output contract
- [x] Measure pixel-area reduction and file-size reduction across all sample screenshots
- [x] Log reduction percentages to a table/CSV for later benchmarking reference

### Phase 5: Validation Testing
- [x] Run `prune()` on all 5–10 sample screenshots without errors or exceptions
- [x] Confirm average reduction falls in the 40–60% target range from the PPT
- [x] Write unit tests for `prune()` covering edge cases (near-blank page, text-dense page)
- [x] Document tuning parameters (threshold value, min contour area) with rationale in code comments

